, Ideas by Rocco Caputo; Tolerance, Understanding, Affection by Terri L. Puckett.\n\nBut maybe include \"Credits 3 people\" as a fact. The detailed credits list shows three people: Sean Michael Puckett, Rocco Caputo, Terri L. Puckett. Actually \"Credits 3 people\" is top summary. The detailed credits includes roles. We can state: The DOS version credits list Sean Michael Puckett for Design, Graphics, and Programming; Rocco Caputo for Testing, Inspiration, and Ideas; and Terri L. Puckett for Tolerance, Understanding, and Affection. That's one finding. Good.\n\nShould we mention publisher? Not asked. Avoid.\n\nPotential issue: \"Released November 1992 on DOS\" date maybe 1992-11. The observation has date: 2004-04-09 at top? That's page date maybe. It says Released November 1992 on DOS. So statement \"Galacta: The Battle for Saturn was released in November 1992 on DOS.\" Good.\n\nMode: \"Business Model Shareware\" and \"Number of Offline Players 1 Player\" and \"Input Devices Supported/Optional Keyboard\". Is \"mode\" meaning gameplay mode? Could be \"Number of Offline Players 1 Player\" and \"Input Devices Supported/Optional Keyboard\". Business model is not mode but release/mode? The OneGap wording: \"Which release, mode and credit facts does the Galacta page establish?\" Maybe mode = business model? We can include \"The page lists the business model as Shareware, one offline player, and keyboard input support.\" That covers.\n\nBut need not enumerate general webpage facts. These directly answer. Good.\n\nNeed final JSON only. Ensure evidence_refs [\"W1\"]. Statements full.\n\nCould there be duplicate? Existing C empty, so no.\n\nNeed maybe finding statement \"Released November 1992 on DOS\" but subject is Galacta. \"Galacta: The Battle for Saturn was released in November 1992 on DOS.\" Evidence W1.\n\nSecond: \"The Galacta page lists the game as shareware, with one offline player and keyboard input support.\" Evidence W1.\n\nThird: \"For the DOS version, the credits